    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6102" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caesor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		caedo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who hews something</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lignorum caesores,</span>”
				<i>hewers of wood</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 53</span></i>
			, n. 6, after the <i><span class="en">Vulg. Deut. 29, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapidum,</span>”
				<i>stone-breaker</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Luc. 2, 89 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Par. 24, 12</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Val.
				Prob. II. p. 1458</span></i> P</div>
